WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:08.164
When Mr. Havisham received Mr. Bennington's letter, he hurried to the castle.

2
00:00:08.165 --> 00:00:17.173
"Finally!" he said to the earl. "We finally have some solid proof that this boy is an imposter."

3
00:00:17.174 --> 00:00:22.694
The earl read Mr. Bennington's letter and looked at the newspaper photo.

4
00:00:22.695 --> 00:00:26.677
"This will be the end of that dreadful woman!"

5
00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:31.551
"She was definitely married to Bevis," Mr. Havisham said.

6
00:00:31.552 --> 00:00:36.190
"But I believe her son is older than she says."

7
00:00:36.191 --> 00:00:40.238
"What are you going to do next?" the earl asked.

8
00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:45.589
"I'll send a cable to Ben and Dick, asking them to come as soon as possible.

9
00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:54.148
I imagine Minna—that's her real name—will be surprised and dismayed to see them."

10
00:00:54.149 --> 00:01:04.393
Mr. Havisham chuckled. "Meanwhile I'll keep pretending that I'm not suspicious of her!"

11
00:01:04.394 --> 00:01:09.945
*** One morning Mr. Havisham and the earl arrived in Minna's sitting room at the

12
00:01:09.946 --> 00:01:15.895
inn. She was sitting on the sofa, making a list of clothes she

13
00:01:15.896 --> 00:01:22.088
required. "The earl and I have brought some old friends to see you," the lawyer

14
00:01:22.089 --> 00:01:27.643
said. "Old friends?" Minna gave him a suspicious

15
00:01:27.644 --> 00:01:33.094
look. "More than friends—family," said Ben, entering the

16
00:01:33.095 --> 00:01:42.193
room. Minna sprang to her feet and cried out in alarm. "I never expected to see you again!"

17
00:01:42.194 --> 00:01:48.684
Mr. Havisham glanced from Ben to Dick. "Do you know her?"

18
00:01:48.685 --> 00:01:56.267
Dick grinned. "Of course we do! Hello, Minna!"

19
00:01:56.268 --> 00:02:01.370
"I'll stand up in any court and say she was my wife," Ben said.

20
00:02:01.371 --> 00:02:06.693
"My brother and her father will also testify that she married me."

21
00:02:06.694 --> 00:02:13.061
"He's lying!" Minna cried. "I've never seen these guys before."

22
00:02:13.062 --> 00:02:17.980
Ben ignored her protests. "Where's our boy, Minna?

23
00:02:17.981 --> 00:02:23.759
I'm through with you and so is he. I'm taking him back to America with me."

24
00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:27.730
At that moment the door leading to the bedroom opened.

25
00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:32.131
A boy who looked just like Ben peeked into the sitting room.

26
00:02:32.132 --> 00:02:37.705
"Look at his chin!" Dick said. "I told you he had a scar."

27
00:02:37.706 --> 00:02:40.935
Everyone peered at the boy's chin.

28
00:02:40.936 --> 00:02:43.490
Ben walked over to him.

29
00:02:43.491 --> 00:02:50.121
"Tom, I'm your father, and I'm taking you with me. Where's your hat?"

30
00:02:50.122 --> 00:02:58.192
The boy pointed to a hat on a chair. Ben picked it up and took Tom by the hand.

31
00:02:58.193 --> 00:03:03.992
"If you need me again, you know where to find me," Ben said to Mr. Havisham.

32
00:03:03.993 --> 00:03:07.257
He left the room without looking at Minna.

33
00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:13.372
"Stop that man! He's kidnapping my son!" Minna screamed.

34
00:03:13.373 --> 00:03:19.510
Just as he'd done before, the earl stayed quiet and stared at Minna.

35
00:03:19.511 --> 00:03:24.255
"We've done some investigating, Minna," Mr. Havisham said.

36
00:03:24.256 --> 00:03:27.829
"We know you abandoned your son years ago.

37
00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:32.269
Recently you took him from the parents who have raised him.

38
00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:37.844
It's time for you to stop harassing the earl and his family."

39
00:03:37.845 --> 00:03:42.985
Full of fury, Minna went into the bedroom and slammed the door.

40
00:03:42.986 --> 00:03:48.811
"She won't dare show her face around here again," Mr. Havisham said.

41
00:03:48.812 --> 00:03:52.762
"If she does, she'll be in trouble with the law.

42
00:03:52.763 --> 00:03:57.511
I'll make sure she's on the next train to London."

43
00:03:57.512 --> 00:04:03.004
"As for you, young man . . ." The earl turned to Dick.

44
00:04:03.005 --> 00:04:05.257
"I'll be forever grateful.

45
00:04:05.258 --> 00:04:10.900
You recognized this imposter and stopped her from breaking up my family."

46
00:04:10.901 --> 00:04:17.973
"Mr. Hobbs and I had to help Cedric, sir," Dick said. "Because everybody likes him!"

47
00:04:17.974 --> 00:04:22.529
"I'll see you at the castle for dinner tonight," the earl said.

48
00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:31.584
"But first I have to tell Lord Fauntleroy—the real Lord Fauntleroy—the good news."

49
00:04:31.585 --> 00:04:37.515
*** When the earl arrived at Mrs. Errol's cottage, she was sitting in the main

50
00:04:37.516 --> 00:04:42.357
room. "Where's Lord Fauntleroy?" the earl asked.

51
00:04:42.358 --> 00:04:49.371
Mrs. Errol stepped forward to greet him. "You mean Cedric is still Lord Fauntleroy?"

52
00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:57.448
"Yes, the matter has been settled." The earl grasped Mrs. Errol's hands in his.

53
00:04:57.449 --> 00:05:02.167
"Cedric! Come quickly!" Mrs. Errol called.

54
00:05:02.168 --> 00:05:05.414
"What is it, Mama? Is something wrong?"

55
00:05:05.415 --> 00:05:10.610
Cedric ran into the room and flung his arms around her neck.

56
00:05:10.611 --> 00:05:14.493
"Hello, Grandpapa! What are you doing here?"

57
00:05:14.494 --> 00:05:22.248
"I've come to tell you the good news. You are the real Lord Fauntleroy."

58
00:05:22.249 --> 00:05:31.215
"Oh, Grandpapa! I'm so glad!" Now it was the earl's turn to receive a hug from Cedric.

59
00:05:31.216 --> 00:05:35.499
"I also want you to do me a favor," the earl said.

60
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:40.308
"Please ask your mother to come with us to the castle."

61
00:05:40.309 --> 00:05:47.233
Cedric's eyes were wide. "Do you mean to live with us?"

62
00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:49.705
The earl nodded.

63
00:05:49.706 --> 00:05:55.842
Mrs. Errol smiled. "Are you sure you want me to do that, my lord?"

64
00:05:55.843 --> 00:06:01.799
"Quite sure!" the earl said. "Please come as soon as possible."

65
00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:09.115
He looked up as Cedric dashed toward the doorway. "Where are you going, Cedric?"

66
00:06:09.116 --> 00:06:15.269
Little Lord Fauntleroy beamed. "To write to my friend Mr. Hobbs.

67
00:06:15.270 --> 00:06:28.055
I want to tell him everything—and invite him to visit us!"

